## Why This Question Is Asked
This question tests understanding of stack augmentation, a practical pattern for maintaining auxiliary state. It demonstrates the ability to design data structures that support efficient queries while handling edge cases like duplicates and empty states.

## Key Concepts
- Two auxiliary stacks (minStack and maxStack) track running minima and maxima in sync with the main stack
- Each push/pop operation updates all three stacks atomically, preserving O(1) time complexity
- Duplicates are handled naturally since the min/max is recalculated at each step
- Empty stack edge cases must be handled (typically by checking stack length before accessing top)

## Code Example
```javascript
class MinMaxStack {
  constructor() {
    this.stack = [];
    this.minStack = [];
    this.maxStack = [];
  }

  push(x) {
    this.stack.push(x);
    this.minStack.push(
      this.minStack.length ? Math.min(x, this.minStack[this.minStack.length - 1]) : x
    );
    this.maxStack.push(
      this.maxStack.length ? Math.max(x, this.maxStack[this.maxStack.length - 1]) : x
    );
  }

  pop() {
    if (this.stack.length === 0) return undefined;
    this.minStack.pop();
    this.maxStack.pop();
    return this.stack.pop();
  }

  top() {
    return this.stack[this.stack.length - 1];
  }

  getMin() {
    return this.minStack[this.minStack.length - 1];
  }

  getMax() {
    return this.maxStack[this.maxStack.length - 1];
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine a hashmap with a priority structure to track a dynamic mode under duplicates, while keeping updates O(log n) on average. It also checks handling of stale entries and edge cases (removals of non-existent values).

## Key Concepts
- Hash map for value-to-count to enable O(1) updates
- Max-heap keyed by (count, -value) to prioritize higher counts and break ties toward smaller values
- Lazy deletion of stale heap entries to keep updates efficient
- Edge cases: removing non-existent values, empty multiset

## Code Example
```javascript
class ModeMultiset {
  constructor() {
    this.cnt = new Map();
    this.heap = []; // max-heap of [count, -value]
  }
  _heapPush(item) { /* standard binary-heap insert with comparator by count desc, value asc */ }
  _heapPop() { /* standard binary-heap extract-max */ }
  addValue(x) {
    const c = (this.cnt.get(x) || 0) + 1;
    this.cnt.set(x, c);
    this._heapPush([c, -x]);
  }
  removeValue(x) {
    const c = this.cnt.get(x);
    if (!c) return;
    const nc = c - 1;
    if (nc > 0) this.cnt.set(x, nc);
    else this.cnt.delete(x);
    if (nc > 0) this._heapPush([nc, -x]);
  }
  getMode() {
    while (this.heap.length) {
      const [c, neg] = this.heap[0];
      const v = -neg;
      if ((this.cnt.get(v) || 0) === c) return v;
      this._heapPop();
    }
    return null;
  }
}
```

